1
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:37,720
[Episode 28]

3
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,070
Wait, why have I suddenly

4
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:41,470
become the main suspect?

5
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,280
Lin Yan was killed because she was

6
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,200
going to see you.

7
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:44,789
And

8
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:46,200
after that,

9
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:48,560
instead of feeling guilty or remorseful,

10
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,590
you hid the truth to protect yourself.

11
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:52,039
That makes you practically an accomplice

12
00:01:52,039 --> 00:01:52,560
to Lin Yan's murder...

13
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,070
No, no! Shut up!

14
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:53,479
Shut up!

15
00:01:53,479 --> 00:01:54,590
Stop talking nonsense!

16
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,890
What kind of reporter are you?

17
00:01:55,890 --> 00:01:56,840
Just watch—I'll sue you!

18
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,770
Go ahead, sue me!

19
00:01:57,950 --> 00:01:58,680
That'll just make me famous!

20
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,229
If I were afraid of that,

21
00:01:59,229 --> 00:02:00,630
I would've quit long ago.

22
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:03,120
Prosecutor Zhang,

23
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,430
aren't you going to stop her?

24
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:05,480
You're just going to
let her act like this?

25
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,480
Isn't she insane?

26
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,480
We don't want to disrupt

27
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,449
your work or family life.

28
00:02:08,449 --> 00:02:09,680
We only care about whether Yan Jicai

29
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,150
was wrongfully convicted.

30
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:12,480
Once the news comes out,

31
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:14,120
you'll be under a lot of pressure

32
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,360
both at home and at work.

33
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,750
You don't need to worry about testifying.

34
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:17,960
Even if the case is retried,

35
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,870
you may not have to appear in court.

36
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:20,960
Even if you didn't
tell the whole truth before,

37
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:21,690
that's fine.

38
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,980
It wouldn't constitute perjury.

39
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,970
You clearly saw the murderer that day.

40
00:02:29,970 --> 00:02:31,000
I didn't!

41
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:32,190
Can you just shut up?

42
00:02:32,210 --> 00:02:33,020
You're lying!

43
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:33,680
You told

44
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,520
a lawyer named Zhou Pu

45
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,430
that you saw with your own eyes

46
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:36,560
that Lin Yan was picked up
by a car that day.

47
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,310
What I told him was...

48
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:37,840
This is his testimony!

49
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,310
That's not what I told him!

50
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,510
I did speak to Zhou Pu!

51
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:46,340
What did you tell him?

52
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:48,120
Tell us.

53
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,750
I said I was drunk.

54
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:56,520
I was groggy,

55
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:58,079
and it felt like I had a dream.

56
00:02:58,079 --> 00:02:59,630
I dreamed that Lin Yan knocked on my door,

57
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:00,760
but I didn't open it.

58
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,680
T-That's all I said.

59
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:06,470
A dream?

60
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:11,540
He told you that himself?

61
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,360
Yes.

62
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:13,870
Around 12:30 that night,

63
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:16,910
Lin Yan went back to Qiao Xiaojun's place
on Shengli Street.

64
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:18,510
Qiao Xiaojun heard knocking

65
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:19,990
but didn't open the door.

66
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:21,430
Xiaojun.

67
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:23,960
Xiaojun!

68
00:03:39,350 --> 00:03:40,430
Then she went downstairs

69
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:41,750
and stood on the street, looking up

70
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:43,810
at Qiao Xiaojun's window for a while.

71
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:45,000
How long did she stand there?

72
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,800
Qiao Xiaojun only glanced once.

73
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:47,630
He was afraid Lin Yan would notice him,

74
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:48,780
so he went back to sleep.

75
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:51,110
So he didn't know
how long she stood there.

76
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,590
So that means

77
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,600
he didn't actually see anything, right?

78
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:03,730
Captain Lyu,

79
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,530
this basically rules out

80
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,190
the possibility
that Yan Jicai committed the crime.

81
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:08,520
It doesn't rule him out.

82
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,800
He could've driven back

83
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,000
and picked Lin Yan up.

84
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,560
Couldn't it have been another taxi?

85
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,960
I'm not saying that's impossible.

86
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,390
But we can't rule out Yan Jicai.

87
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:17,269
In such a short period of time,

88
00:04:17,269 --> 00:04:18,649
how could he possibly have
committed the crime

89
00:04:18,649 --> 00:04:20,190
and then cleaned up the crime scene?

90
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:20,829
His wife said

91
00:04:20,829 --> 00:04:21,920
he came home at...

92
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,830
We can't fully trust

93
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:24,760
his wife's word.

94
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,210
There was DNA

95
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,060
from an unidentified person

96
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,310
under Lin Yan's fingernails.

97
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,360
Eight fingernails.

98
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,680
That wasn't from accidental contact.

99
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,830
There must have been a struggle

100
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:33,700
or close physical contact

101
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:34,870
to leave that behind.

102
00:04:34,870 --> 00:04:35,920
An unidentified person,

103
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,600
Captain Lyu.

104
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,920
-Prosecutor Zhang...
-Maybe...

105
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,980
the real killer is also a taxi driver?

106
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,680
Prosecutor Zhang,

107
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:42,830
we investigated more than

108
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:43,510
100 taxi drivers

109
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:45,240
within a 10-kilometer radius.

110
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:47,480
Yan Jicai was the only suspect
we identified.

111
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,750
What do you think we're here for?

112
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:50,190
You think the police are just for show?

113
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:52,250
The Jia Peng that Yan Jicai mentioned

114
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:53,750
is also a taxi driver.

115
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:54,920
I think we should

116
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,890
compare his DNA

117
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,430
with the DNA found

118
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:58,680
under Lin Yan's fingernails.

119
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,370
What a joke.

120
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,720
You actually believe
what's written in a magazine?

121
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,310
Then the police don't need to

122
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:03,040
investigate crimes anymore.

123
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:03,750
We can just sit at a newsstand

124
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:05,950
and solve cases by reading newspapers.

125
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:10,910
So you're just dead set on
Yan Jicai being the culprit, right?

126
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,630
Anyway, since he's been identified,

127
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:15,690
we can't let him go.

128
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,270
Since he can't be ruled out,

129
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:18,930
we have to pursue it to the end.

130
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:21,270
Otherwise, we'd be failing the victim.

131
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:22,120
Even if we've got the wrong person,

132
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,520
we can't just let them go.

133
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,380
That's a mistake

134
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,550
I'm willing to make.

135
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,330
Letting a guilty person go is one mistake.

136
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:31,620
Wrongfully arresting an innocent person
is two mistakes.

137
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,920
What did you say?

138
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,520
Wronging an innocent person

139
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:36,680
and letting the real culprit get away—

140
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,480
one plus one is greater than two.

141
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:57,230
Wanna see me play an arcade game?

142
00:05:57,270 --> 00:05:58,600
I can beat it on one coin.

143
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:13,040
There's a lot of stuff,
so be careful not to bump into anything.

144
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,120
-Just put it there.
-Thank you.

145
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:14,680
You can put it there.

146
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,280
Thank you.

147
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,310
Dad, Dad,

148
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:29,770
you didn't bring my piano.

149
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,360
Our place is too small now.

150
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:36,520
The piano can't fit.

151
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,390
Let's leave it at Grandpa's for now, okay?

152
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:39,390
When you need to practice the piano,

153
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:40,480
you can go to your teacher's place, okay?

154
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,190
No!

155
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:43,200
Diandian,

156
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:43,830
be good.

157
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,270
Whenever you two used to argue,

158
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:49,420
you'd stop when I played the piano.

159
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,700
Now that there's no piano,

160
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,240
what if you two argue nonstop

161
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:52,920
again?

162
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:58,680
Okay.

163
00:06:59,310 --> 00:07:00,640
We won't argue anymore.

164
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,800
Mom and Dad won't fight anymore,

165
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,190
okay?

166
00:07:06,070 --> 00:07:06,800
Pinky swear.

167
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:08,800
You can't argue anymore, understand?

168
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,330
We won't.

169
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,140
Alright?

170
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,870
Put your bag in your room. Go on.

171
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:16,720
Have you told Diandian

172
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,050
about going to Beijing?

173
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:21,970
I will.

174
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,200
I'll tell her myself.

175
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,450
I'm just grabbing a few things.

176
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:42,870
What's this?

177
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:44,560
Internet.

178
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:46,230
What "Internet"?

179
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:47,980
Just going online.

180
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,690
Isn't Feng Feng working at China Telecom?

181
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:51,270
I had him

182
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:52,090
install this for me.

183
00:07:52,090 --> 00:07:54,220
Once it's connected to the phone line,
I can use it.

184
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,430
I'm going to register an email address.

185
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,600
Foreign companies are all using it now.

186
00:07:55,690 --> 00:07:57,350
[Beijing Oumai
Advertising & Communications Co., Ltd.]

187
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,800
That classmate of yours in Beijing?

188
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:01,600
Yes.

189
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,480
Go ahead.

190
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,510
Qin,

191
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:15,980
we're heading out.

192
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:16,870
Thank you.

193
00:08:17,190 --> 00:08:17,600
Um...

194
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,190
Goodbye, Mr. Qin.

195
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:19,390
Take your time. Bye.

196
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,400
That was so awkward.

197
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:26,630
A whole table full of food,

198
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:28,130
and only the three of us showed up.

199
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:28,890
Qin has been

200
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,980
getting a bit full of himself lately.

201
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:33,159
He's quite pitiful.

202
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,240
Sir,

203
00:08:38,669 --> 00:08:40,200
we've canceled
the rest of the dishes for you.

204
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,390
There are still 2 dishes being cooked,
so we can't cancel those.

205
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:44,250
Here are 15 takeaway containers.

206
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,240
Qin,

207
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:59,270
why didn't you tell me you were coming?

208
00:08:59,270 --> 00:08:59,770
It's our own restaurant!

209
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:01,300
I can give you a discount!

210
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,630
T-There's so much food left.

211
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:05,240
Zeming.

212
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,260
I'm rich now.

213
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,840
I'm here to support your business.

214
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,900
I don't want to take advantage of you.

215
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:12,510
Your wife didn't come?

216
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:13,840
No.

217
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,450
Forget I asked. Forget I asked.

218
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:22,670
Zeming.

219
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,010
Here in Nanyu...

220
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:30,750
you're the only one who's so nice

221
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:32,350
to me and thinks highly of me.

222
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,000
Tell me,

223
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:35,150
what do I have to do

224
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:38,380
to get people to actually respect me?

225
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,470
What's wrong?

226
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,720
I made some money

227
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,350
and wanted to treat everyone
to a good meal.

228
00:09:44,350 --> 00:09:46,010
I spent several hundred yuan,

229
00:09:46,030 --> 00:09:48,210
and only 3 people from the firm showed up.

230
00:09:48,210 --> 00:09:50,010
Even Li Xiang didn't come for me.

231
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,080
Mr. Qin,

232
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:53,550
don't overthink it.

233
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:54,270
Everyone's probably got stuff going on.

234
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:55,730
They're busy, that's all.

235
00:09:58,550 --> 00:09:59,200
Well...

236
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,150
I-I'll have the staff pack the dishes up

237
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:02,630
for you to take home, alright?

238
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:03,240
No, no, no.

239
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,360
If my wife finds out

240
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,360
I wasted this much money,

241
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:10,140
we'll end up fighting again.

242
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,320
Forget it.

243
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,290
Throw them away.

244
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:17,960
I'm off.

245
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,960
Qin, be careful.

246
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,200
Gu.

247
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,520
Tell the cashier—

248
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:46,240
waive his bill
and give him his money back.

249
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:46,870
Boss,

250
00:10:47,670 --> 00:10:49,730
you give away free meals every day...

251
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:50,720
Go on.

252
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,030
Okay.

253
00:10:52,510 --> 00:10:53,030
If you don't mind,

254
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,360
you can all eat it later.

255
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:02,240
Hello.

256
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:03,870
Gaoyuan.

257
00:11:04,550 --> 00:11:05,080
Go ahead.

258
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:06,960
Oumai

259
00:11:07,510 --> 00:11:09,640
is a Chinese-American joint venture.

260
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,500
Go help me look into it.

261
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,630
Why do you want to look into that company?

262
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:14,720
What kind of information?

263
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,910
Its qualifications, that sort of thing.

264
00:11:15,910 --> 00:11:17,630
Just ask around
and find out as much as you can.

265
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:18,030
Okay?

266
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:18,720
Okay.

267
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,280
Okay, I'm hanging up.

268
00:12:04,550 --> 00:12:06,010
If you don't want me to see,

269
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,640
take all those down from the wall first.

270
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:13,960
How is it?

271
00:12:14,670 --> 00:12:15,930
Did you find anything?

272
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,760
We can't discuss the case.

273
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,420
Didn't I already tell you?

274
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:26,080
You haven't gone out these past few days?

275
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:26,630
No.

276
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,390
If I don't come,

277
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:30,520
you won't even eat properly, will you?

278
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:32,430
Eat up.

279
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:34,100
It'll get cold.

280
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,510
You're completely obsessed.

281
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:39,370
Have you eaten?

282
00:12:39,510 --> 00:12:40,030
Yeah.

283
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:41,550
Okay.

284
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:49,720
Actually, you don't have to

285
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,270
stay in Binjiang all the time.

286
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,550
Go back to Beijing first.

287
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:54,350
Come back if something comes up.

288
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:56,870
I can't bear to leave.

289
00:12:58,750 --> 00:12:59,680
I'm telling you,

290
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:01,600
this period I've spent here

291
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,840
has been the happiest

292
00:13:03,630 --> 00:13:04,390
and least

293
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,780
stressful time of my life.

294
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:10,510
Pathetic.

295
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:18,990
Now that you're here,

296
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,440
it's killing me

297
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,910
not to talk about the case with you.

298
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:22,910
It's killing you?

299
00:13:25,510 --> 00:13:26,720
Call Lu over then.

300
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,620
If he comes,

301
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:31,950
he'll definitely keep you up every night.

302
00:13:32,570 --> 00:13:33,200
Sure.

303
00:13:37,910 --> 00:13:39,390
I told you both, didn't I?

304
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:43,100
I said I was all for you
opening a restaurant,

305
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:44,320
but you were not to serve anyone

306
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:46,030
from the political or legal system.

307
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:46,630
So you just ignored

308
00:13:46,630 --> 00:13:47,600
what I said?

309
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:48,790
Well,

310
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,860
that's just not practical.

311
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,890
How would we know who everyone is?

312
00:13:52,930 --> 00:13:54,190
We can't exactly check

313
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,510
every customer's work ID, right?

314
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:55,870
Dad,

315
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,210
we're running

316
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,600
a legitimate restaurant.

317
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,100
Everything is clearly priced.

318
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:01,960
If an old acquaintance comes by

319
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,560
and we give them a discount,
isn't that normal?

320
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,480
My school was shut down, so I couldn't get
a permanent government position.

321
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,030
And I'm pregnant.

322
00:14:07,030 --> 00:14:08,480
I'm just trying to earn a living,

323
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,240
and you keep saying this won't do,

324
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:09,750
that won't do.

325
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:11,350
What am I supposed to do then?

326
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:14,930
Zeming has asked me over and over

327
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:15,990
to move to Beijing.

328
00:14:16,550 --> 00:14:17,600
But I didn't go.

329
00:14:17,630 --> 00:14:18,720
Because I wanted to stay here

330
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:19,780
and look after you.

331
00:14:21,550 --> 00:14:23,210
You're being way too selfish.

332
00:14:31,270 --> 00:14:32,470
Go comfort your wife.

333
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,690
Whoever made her cry should deal with it.

334
00:14:34,690 --> 00:14:35,350
I got a call.

335
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:36,320
What did you say?

336
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,650
Hello, Yizhong.

337
00:14:42,270 --> 00:14:43,750
How's the case going over there?

338
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,550
To be honest, I really want to go.

339
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:46,630
I'm stuck here all day

340
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,000
watching a bunch of cooks

341
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:48,840
and waiters—

342
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:50,590
I'm practically growing mold.

343
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:51,690
What?

344
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:52,960
What could possibly be so urgent

345
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,150
that it has to be me?

346
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,480
What, it'll fall apart without me?

347
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:00,810
Well, I absolutely cannot go!

348
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:02,410
Ding Rui's pregnant right now!

349
00:15:02,410 --> 00:15:05,140
What could possibly
be more important than that?

350
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:08,080
Exactly!

351
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,090
My wife

352
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:10,440
and family come first!

353
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:11,320
Then let it fall apart!

354
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,630
Let the whole thing go to hell!

355
00:15:12,630 --> 00:15:14,120
Enough, cut it out.

356
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:16,840
Get lost

357
00:15:16,870 --> 00:15:18,400
and go find your best buddy.

358
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:19,950
Thank you, darling.

359
00:15:19,950 --> 00:15:21,030
I'll be there the day after tomorrow.

360
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:22,360
The day after tomorrow.

361
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:22,870
Honey.

362
00:15:24,150 --> 00:15:25,680
Honey, I'm all yours today.

363
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:32,410
Got her to sleep?

364
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:38,200
This is what's left over from Diandian's

365
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,600
one-month celebration.

366
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:48,870
I'm sorry.

367
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,730
Before, I pressured you...

368
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,660
into helping my dad's old comrade-in-arms.

369
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:56,750
I only found out later

370
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:58,200
that he was involved in
not only civil disputes

371
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,730
but also financial issues.

372
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,360
In there, he was
throwing his weight around,

373
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,290
saying that you,

374
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,790
the deputy president of the court,
were practically his son-in-law,

375
00:16:06,790 --> 00:16:08,790
and he almost dragged you into this.

376
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,360
I really didn't know

377
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,800
he was that kind of person before.

378
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:13,530
If I'd known,

379
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:15,680
I never would've asked you to help him.

380
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:23,580
Then...

381
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,500
how is the court planning to deal with it?

382
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,390
They had me in for a talk a few days ago,

383
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:29,720
and I explained myself.

384
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:32,270
Worst case, I'll face disciplinary action.
It's nothing.

385
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:32,790
No.

386
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:35,630
Why should you face disciplinary action?

387
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:36,360
All these years,

388
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,200
you've handled

389
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,510
so many difficult cases.

390
00:16:38,510 --> 00:16:39,750
Every commendation you've received

391
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,550
was earned through your own hard work.

392
00:16:41,550 --> 00:16:42,870
Court Pres. Qiu can't just

393
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:44,120
punish you because some scoundrel

394
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,050
tried to drag you

395
00:16:45,150 --> 00:16:46,670
into his mess.

396
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:49,270
That's a bit much—just casting you aside
after everything you've done for them.

397
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:50,150
They need to do something to show

398
00:16:50,150 --> 00:16:52,450
people outside that they're taking action.

399
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:53,240
Besides, I didn't actually
do anything wrong,

400
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,770
so there's no need to worry.

401
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:01,450
I don't want you to suffer because of me.

402
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:07,050
There's no point talking about that now.

403
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:08,599
Have you finished packing?

404
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,740
There are still a few things left.

405
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,599
I can sort them out before I leave.

406
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:21,470
You're staying with Diandian tonight?

407
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:39,670
[Nanlu Public Security Bureau]

408
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:39,810
This man is Jia Peng.

409
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,490
He used to drive a taxi here.

410
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:44,070
He committed his crime in Jiangbei.

411
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:46,670
They even came here
to investigate at the time.

412
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,550
He committed a crime in Jiangbei?

413
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:48,920
Yes.

414
00:17:50,070 --> 00:17:51,470
So we should investigate

415
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:53,350
whether Jia Peng was here

416
00:17:53,350 --> 00:17:55,150
when Yan Jicai's case happened.

417
00:17:57,170 --> 00:17:57,740
Mentor,

418
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:58,830
you're really fixated on

419
00:17:58,830 --> 00:17:59,730
this case.

420
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:03,410
You even believe rumors and hearsay?

421
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:05,720
It's common
for serious offenders in prison

422
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,250
to claim they're innocent.

423
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:12,810
Is it really that hard to look into it?

424
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:24,200
Hello, is Zhang Hongshan there?

425
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,280
Tell him to see me when he comes back.

426
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:27,250
That's all.

427
00:18:30,070 --> 00:18:30,640
Mentor,

428
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:33,060
he's gone to the western suburbs.

429
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,640
Would you like to wait here

430
00:18:35,310 --> 00:18:36,440
or come another day?

431
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:37,790
What?

432
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:39,610
Sick of me already?

433
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,240
Of course not.

434
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,510
You could sit here all day,

435
00:18:44,510 --> 00:18:45,640
and I still wouldn't be annoyed.

436
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,300
Seeing how energetic you are,

437
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:48,810
I couldn't be happier.

438
00:18:50,510 --> 00:18:51,040
Alright.

439
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,860
Then let me ask you something.

440
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,200
If Jia Peng really was here

441
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,000
when Yan Jicai's case occurred,

442
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,040
what would you do?

443
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,970
I'd like to hear your thoughts.

444
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:06,750
Do you remember

445
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:07,650
the DNA found

446
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,680
in the skin tissue

447
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,350
under all 8 of Lin Yan's fingernails?

448
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,810
I think we should compare it.

449
00:19:11,810 --> 00:19:12,850
You're asking me

450
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,540
to reopen the investigation.

451
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:18,030
This case

452
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,130
caused a huge sensation back then.

453
00:19:21,550 --> 00:19:24,000
If we overturn everything and start again,

454
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,340
the fallout will be even greater.

455
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:28,160
Finding fault

456
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:28,810
is the easiest thing

457
00:19:28,810 --> 00:19:29,810
in the world.

458
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,270
To deny the past based purely on

459
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:32,920
personal speculation

460
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:33,790
and inference—

461
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:36,520
wouldn't that be disrespectful

462
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:37,960
to all the grassroots officers
who worked so hard

463
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:38,690
on this case?

464
00:19:39,270 --> 00:19:40,800
Wouldn't that also suggest

465
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,680
that there were serious problems

466
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,010
with our previous work?

467
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,350
Indeed.

468
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:47,550
To prove a wrongful conviction,

469
00:19:47,550 --> 00:19:49,640
either new evidence must be discovered,

470
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,480
or the supposedly dead victim

471
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:54,310
must turn out to be alive
and suddenly return,

472
00:19:54,310 --> 00:19:57,400
or the real perpetrator
must turn out to be someone else.

473
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,110
But so far,

474
00:19:58,720 --> 00:19:59,750
none of those things have happened

475
00:19:59,750 --> 00:20:00,510
in this case.

476
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,340
Lyu Tiancheng mentioned that

477
00:20:05,550 --> 00:20:06,370
when Yan Jicai's case

478
00:20:06,370 --> 00:20:07,040
happened,

479
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:08,330
Jia Peng was also here.

480
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:08,920
Also,

481
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:10,960
the witness back then, Qiao Xiaojun,

482
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:14,070
concealed important timing information
during the trial.

483
00:20:14,070 --> 00:20:15,730
For the sake of a fair verdict,

484
00:20:15,890 --> 00:20:17,350
I think it's necessary for us to compare

485
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:18,150
Jia Peng's DNA

486
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:19,490
with the DNA

487
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,750
from the skin tissue found

488
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:22,610
under the victim's fingernails.

489
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,750
Has it been confirmed
that this so-called Jia Peng

490
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:26,480
was actually here
at the time of the crime?

491
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,400
We've checked.

492
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:29,110
He was indeed here.

493
00:20:33,550 --> 00:20:34,680
Personally, I think

494
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:36,160
the law is no joke.

495
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:38,590
We cannot be influenced
by gossip magazines

496
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:40,750
or by prisoners claiming
that they've been wrongfully convicted.

497
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:41,680
Nor can we allow those things

498
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,310
to sway us.

499
00:20:43,310 --> 00:20:46,480
We need to be extremely cautious
when reopening the investigation.

500
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,280
Extremely cautious, comrades.

501
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,920
You're here already?

502
00:21:08,110 --> 00:21:09,970
I came by plane.

503
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,530
I missed you so much, buddy!

504
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,170
Come in.

505
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:13,680
Come on.

506
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,720
Good lord.

507
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,750
Let's go. My goodness...

508
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:23,510
I...

509
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:24,400
Hurry.

510
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:25,830
Let's go. Go.

511
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:26,510
Go.

512
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:30,930
Xia Yingjie.

513
00:21:32,150 --> 00:21:32,880
Xia Yingjie!

514
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:33,960
Coming.

515
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:34,380
Hurry.

516
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:37,830
What are you two doing?

517
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:39,160
T-This way.

518
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,160
Come on, this way.

519
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:43,200
Important evidence.

520
00:21:45,070 --> 00:21:45,930
Put it in there.

521
00:21:48,550 --> 00:21:49,880
Quite a variety, huh?

522
00:21:50,030 --> 00:21:50,590
I've been working here

523
00:21:50,590 --> 00:21:51,130
for years.

524
00:21:51,130 --> 00:21:52,240
You think I can't
get my hands on this stuff?

525
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,970
Don't ask questions. Pick one.

526
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,770
Go ahead and stab it.

527
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:01,820
Hold it firmly.

528
00:22:02,310 --> 00:22:02,970
Be careful.

529
00:22:17,070 --> 00:22:18,000
Try another one?

530
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:18,680
Yeah.

531
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,840
That's about enough.

532
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,030
Yizhong, stop studying it.

533
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:41,590
Let's eat something.

534
00:22:41,590 --> 00:22:42,750
Yes, eat first.

535
00:22:42,750 --> 00:22:44,150
The food is getting cold.

536
00:22:44,590 --> 00:22:46,830
This half a pig—we'll be eating it
through New Year's, huh?

537
00:22:46,830 --> 00:22:48,750
Why do I always seem to
have some connection with pigs?

538
00:22:48,750 --> 00:22:49,810
Here, have a piece.

539
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,400
You didn't stew the piece
I stabbed, did you?

540
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,400
I'm not stupid.

541
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,720
How would I dare touch it
without your permission?

542
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,240
Why do you two sound

543
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,770
like an old married couple?

544
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,830
When is Ding Rui due?

545
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,310
In a while.

546
00:23:04,310 --> 00:23:06,770
Otherwise, could I just
come over like this?

547
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:11,000
So you're just not handling
Mr. Yuan's side of things anymore?

548
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,070
As for the non-litigation work,

549
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:15,200
my people are running it pretty smoothly.

550
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:16,480
If he doesn't come to me,

551
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,670
I'll just pretend I don't see it.

552
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:18,330
I'll take it

553
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:19,810
as charity work.

554
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:22,710
I've made some soup too.

555
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:29,310
Together now?

556
00:23:29,790 --> 00:23:30,720
What do you mean?

557
00:23:35,490 --> 00:23:36,100
Come here.

558
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,110
If you

559
00:23:43,110 --> 00:23:44,970
were going to kill someone today,

560
00:23:45,750 --> 00:23:46,680
which one of these weapons

561
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,680
would you choose?

562
00:23:48,250 --> 00:23:49,760
If I were Xia Yingjie,

563
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:51,510
I definitely wouldn't choose you.

564
00:23:51,510 --> 00:23:53,770
Boring, dull, and unpleasant to look at.

565
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:55,550
I'm having you pick a weapon,

566
00:23:55,550 --> 00:23:56,310
not pick me.

567
00:23:56,330 --> 00:23:57,590
Fine, fine. I'll pick.

568
00:23:58,830 --> 00:23:59,360
This one.

569
00:24:00,590 --> 00:24:01,640
Concealable, easy to carry,

570
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:02,970
and comfortable to use.

571
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:03,840
Right?

572
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:06,680
Then which one wouldn't you choose?

573
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:08,030
This one, for sure.

574
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:10,110
The blade is too long,
and the handle is too short.

575
00:24:10,110 --> 00:24:11,640
This guard here gets in the way.

576
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:12,640
It's hard to grip.

577
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:13,880
It's not convenient.

578
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,810
That's what I think too.

579
00:24:21,090 --> 00:24:21,680
Hey, man!

580
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:23,070
Hey, what are you doing?

581
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:24,880
What are you doing?

582
00:24:25,070 --> 00:24:25,880
Look, look!

583
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,380
You grabbed it in one move.

584
00:24:27,510 --> 00:24:29,570
You could barely stab anyone with it.

585
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:33,000
If you'd just killed someone,

586
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:35,510
would you bring
the murder weapon home with you?

587
00:24:35,510 --> 00:24:36,240
With my IQ,

588
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,200
I definitely wouldn't bring it back.

589
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,600
I can't speak for others.

590
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:41,280
Well, what exactly
are you trying to prove?

591
00:24:41,450 --> 00:24:43,200
I think the weapon used to kill Yin Ping

592
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,810
may not necessarily
have been a triangular bayonet.

593
00:24:44,810 --> 00:24:46,160
But didn't the autopsy report say

594
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:47,490
the wound matched?

595
00:24:48,310 --> 00:24:49,400
"The features are distinctive,

596
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,860
and the shape is unusual."

597
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:52,590
It states "basically a match."

598
00:24:52,590 --> 00:24:53,000
Look.

599
00:24:54,750 --> 00:24:56,830
Although the bayonet has a flat tip,

600
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,030
it does leave a triangular puncture

601
00:24:59,030 --> 00:25:00,560
when it pierces something.

602
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:01,810
Now look at this.

603
00:25:03,110 --> 00:25:04,750
This was made by stabbing
with a triangular scraper.

604
00:25:04,750 --> 00:25:07,160
This wound matches
the one from the bayonet too.

605
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,690
So you're saying the weapon

606
00:25:08,790 --> 00:25:09,880
that killed Yin Ping

607
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:12,280
could also have been a triangular scraper?

608
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:13,000
Yeah.

609
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,260
Come on, Lihui.

610
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:29,020
Let's eat here.

611
00:25:29,350 --> 00:25:31,210
Aren't we going to Guiya's place?

612
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:32,560
I still want to talk to her.

613
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:34,000
I want to find out exactly what time

614
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:35,200
Yan Jicai went home that night.

615
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,800
Maybe there are other clues.

616
00:25:37,610 --> 00:25:38,940
I've been craving this.

617
00:25:39,590 --> 00:25:39,990
Ma'am.

618
00:25:40,270 --> 00:25:41,550
Two bowls of pickled-cabbage rice noodles.

619
00:25:41,550 --> 00:25:42,750
One spicy, one not spicy.

620
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:44,150
Add meat to the spicy one.

621
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,440
Would you like a fried egg?

622
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:45,790
Okay.

623
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:47,140
And another fried egg.

624
00:25:47,750 --> 00:25:48,350
Thank you.

625
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,240
Sure thing, coming right up.

626
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:10,510
After eating,

627
00:26:10,510 --> 00:26:11,750
we can still make the 8:30 showing

628
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:12,440
of Mission: Impossible.

629
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,770
A foreign blockbuster.

630
00:26:15,830 --> 00:26:16,360
Jianmin,

631
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:19,030
what's your take

632
00:26:19,030 --> 00:26:20,290
on this case right now?

633
00:26:21,070 --> 00:26:22,270
Let's put it aside for the moment.

634
00:26:22,270 --> 00:26:24,070
Come watch a movie with me, okay?

635
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:26,580
Did someone say something to you?

636
00:26:26,790 --> 00:26:27,320
Nothing.

637
00:26:29,830 --> 00:26:30,830
Really, nothing.

638
00:26:37,510 --> 00:26:38,200
Xiaowen.

639
00:26:39,510 --> 00:26:40,830
Then... I'm leaving.

640
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,160
Keep

641
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:43,680
this money.

642
00:26:47,790 --> 00:26:49,520
Where'd you get all this money?

643
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:52,760
My practice has been
doing pretty well lately.

644
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:55,580
I don't want it.

645
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:59,220
It's useless for me to keep the money.

646
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:01,530
It's all going to be yours eventually.

647
00:27:04,830 --> 00:27:07,440
W-When Pei is a little older,

648
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,240
bring the child

649
00:27:09,790 --> 00:27:10,830
and move back home,

650
00:27:10,830 --> 00:27:11,400
okay?

651
00:27:14,790 --> 00:27:15,440
Xiaowen,

652
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:18,150
your mom and I really didn't know

653
00:27:18,270 --> 00:27:20,240
he was disabled back then.

654
00:27:22,070 --> 00:27:23,240
What do we have to do

655
00:27:23,270 --> 00:27:23,920
for you to forgive...

656
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,180
Enough, stop talking.

657
00:27:34,330 --> 00:27:35,860
Be careful on your way home.

658
00:28:03,170 --> 00:28:04,030
Come on, hurry.

659
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,350
Why watch a movie?

660
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:06,510
The tickets are so expensive.

661
00:28:06,510 --> 00:28:08,880
We can buy 2 bags of peanuts
with that money.

662
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:10,440
Just think of it as us having
a little husband-and-wife time.

663
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:12,100
What husband-and-wife time?

664
00:28:12,510 --> 00:28:14,170
You're up to something again?

665
00:28:14,620 --> 00:28:15,880
What are you thinking?

666
00:28:16,680 --> 00:28:17,640
If we don't get along,

667
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:18,830
our daughter won't be willing to

668
00:28:18,830 --> 00:28:19,830
come live with us.

669
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:22,880
It's my fault
that Xiaowen doesn't want to come back?

670
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:24,640
You're useless,
and you're blaming me for it?

671
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:25,590
Alright, alright.

672
00:28:25,590 --> 00:28:26,200
It's my fault.

673
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:26,800
Mr. Qin,

674
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:28,910
you're here to watch a movie too?

675
00:28:29,070 --> 00:28:29,600
Let's go.

676
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:30,610
Who was that?

677
00:28:30,790 --> 00:28:31,440
A client.

678
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:32,780
Come on, hurry.

679
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:36,500
Hurry, come on.

680
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:45,880
If you really want a divorce,

681
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:47,010
you need a lawyer.

682
00:28:47,270 --> 00:28:48,600
Look, I hired Qin Zhigao

683
00:28:48,750 --> 00:28:49,400
to write the complaint.

684
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,730
It only cost me 450 yuan.

685
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:52,440
His rates are that low?

686
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,350
He's just a pushover.

687
00:28:53,350 --> 00:28:54,440
I said a few words,

688
00:28:54,590 --> 00:28:56,190
and he eagerly took the case.

689
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,860
That's why we all call him
a spineless pushover.

690
00:28:59,510 --> 00:29:00,710
Spineless pushover.

691
00:29:00,790 --> 00:29:01,990
Spineless pushover.

692
00:29:03,940 --> 00:29:05,980
Who are you calling a spineless pushover?

693
00:29:05,980 --> 00:29:08,310
Who are you calling a spineless pushover?

694
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:09,590
What do you want?

695
00:29:09,590 --> 00:29:10,350
What are you doing?

696
00:29:10,350 --> 00:29:11,160
Let go!

697
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:11,860
Go to hell!

698
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:17,140
You have to beat her up for me!

699
00:29:17,140 --> 00:29:19,200
If you don't hit her, you're not a man!

700
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:37,360
This lotus pond is so beautiful.

701
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:43,830
What?

702
00:29:45,070 --> 00:29:47,030
Now you don't even dare

703
00:29:47,030 --> 00:29:48,360
invite me to the bureau?

704
00:29:48,750 --> 00:29:51,000
As long as I'm in office
for even one more day,

705
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:51,790
the door of our bureau

706
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:53,250
will always be open to you.

707
00:29:54,550 --> 00:29:55,960
Mainly, we can say

708
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:57,330
whatever we want here.

709
00:30:01,110 --> 00:30:02,070
Was Jia Peng here

710
00:30:02,070 --> 00:30:03,800
when the crime occurred or not?

711
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:08,720
I'm really quite worried about you.

712
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:10,110
Look.

713
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:12,160
You had a child later in life.
It wasn't easy.

714
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:13,510
And she's in the hospital now.

715
00:30:13,510 --> 00:30:14,970
And your wife doesn't have a job.

716
00:30:14,970 --> 00:30:15,720
And the work you do at the arcade

717
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:17,550
is just helping a friend for free.

718
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:20,480
Is your retirement pension
really enough to live on?

719
00:30:21,510 --> 00:30:22,000
What?

720
00:30:22,590 --> 00:30:23,400
Are you going to

721
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:24,730
rehire me at the bureau?

722
00:30:24,860 --> 00:30:26,390
I'm fine with it. I can do it.

723
00:30:26,830 --> 00:30:28,960
Well, I've really thought about that.

724
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:31,740
But I don't have the authority to decide.

725
00:30:31,790 --> 00:30:32,350
How about

726
00:30:32,790 --> 00:30:33,960
I find you a company

727
00:30:34,830 --> 00:30:37,200
where you could work as a consultant
or something?

728
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,160
First, it'd give you something to do.

729
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:41,070
Second, it'd give you
a little extra income, right?

730
00:30:41,070 --> 00:30:43,590
Alright, you don't need to
worry about those things.

731
00:30:43,590 --> 00:30:45,120
I'll only ask you one thing.

732
00:30:45,790 --> 00:30:46,880
Was Jia Peng

733
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:48,740
in Nanlu when the crime happened?

734
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,310
This tea is really good.

735
00:30:50,310 --> 00:30:50,830
Mentor, try it...

736
00:30:50,830 --> 00:30:53,160
Don't change the subject. I'm asking you!

737
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:55,830
He was!

738
00:30:57,550 --> 00:30:58,030
Yes!

739
00:31:02,600 --> 00:31:04,200
Then what are you going to do?

740
00:31:04,590 --> 00:31:06,680
What I want to do doesn't matter.

741
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,040
I told you a long time ago.

742
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:12,260
You're up against the entire system.

743
00:31:12,510 --> 00:31:14,110
Even if you drag me into this,

744
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:14,790
the result would just be

745
00:31:14,790 --> 00:31:15,830
one more poor soul, that's all.

746
00:31:15,830 --> 00:31:17,090
Don't you understand?

747
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:19,080
I understand. I understand.

748
00:31:19,310 --> 00:31:21,240
I promise I won't bother you again.

749
00:31:22,350 --> 00:31:23,680
I'm sorry. I've caused you trouble.

750
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:25,270
Come on, what do you mean by this?

751
00:31:25,270 --> 00:31:25,790
I know.

752
00:31:26,570 --> 00:31:27,400
I'm retired now.

753
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,640
I'm old. I'm nobody anymore.

754
00:31:28,640 --> 00:31:30,700
I shouldn't be causing trouble here.

755
00:31:31,310 --> 00:31:32,510
But I have my dignity.

756
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:33,160
Mentor!

757
00:31:34,790 --> 00:31:35,750
Do you really think Yan Jicai

758
00:31:35,750 --> 00:31:36,790
was wrongfully convicted?

759
00:31:36,790 --> 00:31:37,440
We worked on

760
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:38,030
this case together!

761
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:38,400
No.

762
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,000
To this day, I still believe

763
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:41,590
Yan Jicai is the real murderer.

764
00:31:41,590 --> 00:31:42,550
I'm not asking for anything else.

765
00:31:42,550 --> 00:31:43,330
I'm only asking

766
00:31:43,330 --> 00:31:44,510
for a DNA comparison.

767
00:31:44,510 --> 00:31:45,350
If it proves that the DNA

768
00:31:45,350 --> 00:31:46,270
wasn't Jia Peng's,

769
00:31:46,270 --> 00:31:48,130
wouldn't that settle the matter?

770
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,740
Do we really not even
have the confidence to do that?

771
00:31:52,310 --> 00:31:53,240
What a joke.

772
00:31:59,280 --> 00:31:59,930
Lihui!

773
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:01,450
You're back!

774
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:02,980
Go wash your hands.

775
00:32:04,750 --> 00:32:06,210
You made all these dishes?

776
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,610
The cold dishes are store-bought.

777
00:32:10,110 --> 00:32:10,790
No wonder you didn't wait for me

778
00:32:10,790 --> 00:32:12,720
and come home together after work.

779
00:32:13,590 --> 00:32:15,410
I took half a day off in advance.

780
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:17,920
From now on, we should

781
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:19,110
leave work separately.

782
00:32:19,110 --> 00:32:21,240
Minimize contact as much as possible.

783
00:32:21,470 --> 00:32:23,790
I've just been transferred here
from Bieshan.

784
00:32:23,790 --> 00:32:25,650
I'm afraid it might be bad for you.

785
00:32:27,310 --> 00:32:28,370
Go wash your hands.

786
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:33,580
Don't pour too much.

787
00:32:35,590 --> 00:32:36,160
Cheers!

788
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:41,060
Take it easy.

789
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,860
Haven't you heard the saying?

790
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:43,790
"Once a woman

791
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:46,430
dares to pick up a wine glass,

792
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,730
she can really put it away."

793
00:32:49,070 --> 00:32:49,920
Okay, okay.

794
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:51,590
Don't drink too much.

795
00:32:51,590 --> 00:32:53,050
You have to work tomorrow.

796
00:32:55,070 --> 00:32:56,870
I just feel like drinking today.

797
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:58,350
You know what?

798
00:32:58,350 --> 00:32:59,850
Back when we were in college,

799
00:32:59,850 --> 00:33:00,910
different classes

800
00:33:01,030 --> 00:33:02,310
competed in drinking contests.

801
00:33:02,310 --> 00:33:03,830
I was the hope of our class.

802
00:33:04,590 --> 00:33:05,720
The nuclear weapon!

803
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,320
Don't underestimate me!

804
00:33:07,630 --> 00:33:08,680
I just... bam!

805
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,720
I drank them all under the table!

806
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:11,720
Drink!

807
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,460
No, no, no. Alright.

808
00:33:13,460 --> 00:33:15,110
We really shouldn't drink anymore.

809
00:33:15,110 --> 00:33:16,160
Listen to me; we really should stop.

810
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,270
We have to work tomorrow.

811
00:33:17,270 --> 00:33:18,030
Give it to me!

812
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:19,440
What are you doing?

813
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,700
Seriously, we shouldn't drink anymore.

814
00:33:23,110 --> 00:33:24,000
What's wrong?

815
00:33:26,390 --> 00:33:26,920
Don't drink straight from the bottle!

816
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:27,680
Give it to me!

817
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:28,680
You really shouldn't drink like this.

818
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:29,740
Careful, careful.

819
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,280
No, no, the floor is cold.

820
00:33:34,860 --> 00:33:35,520
Be careful.

821
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:42,720
What's wrong?

822
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:46,160
I'm sorry.

823
00:33:52,720 --> 00:33:54,780
I've put you in a difficult position.

824
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:56,590
No.

825
00:33:58,550 --> 00:34:00,210
The court transferred me here

826
00:34:00,550 --> 00:34:02,510
to bring the two of us together.

827
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:03,790
I know.

828
00:34:04,590 --> 00:34:06,450
I should've been understanding.

829
00:34:09,330 --> 00:34:10,320
I shouldn't have been like this,

830
00:34:10,320 --> 00:34:11,520
causing you trouble.

831
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:13,380
I should've been content.

832
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:15,280
I also know...

833
00:34:16,190 --> 00:34:17,790
you're doing all this for me—

834
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,800
simply because of me,

835
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:21,280
not for Yan Jicai at all.

836
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:22,139
I know all that.

837
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:24,000
It's both.

838
00:34:24,580 --> 00:34:25,969
I don't know why either.

839
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,070
I just can't hold it back. I feel awful.

840
00:34:28,070 --> 00:34:29,670
I feel so suffocated inside.

841
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:30,889
I don't know

842
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:32,710
how to let it out.

843
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,230
I miss my mentor.

844
00:34:45,030 --> 00:34:46,760
I miss my mentor.

845
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:48,510
Jianmin...

846
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:52,880
Should I not have done this?

847
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:56,030
No, no, no.

848
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:58,250
I shouldn't have done this, right?

849
00:35:08,070 --> 00:35:08,670
Kiss me.

850
00:35:11,550 --> 00:35:13,080
I just vomited. It's dirty.

851
00:35:13,550 --> 00:35:15,680
I want to kiss you even if you're dirty.

852
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:27,240
I feel much better after crying.

853
00:35:28,590 --> 00:35:29,520
All these years,

854
00:35:30,190 --> 00:35:31,790
I've never vented like this.

855
00:35:35,110 --> 00:35:36,910
Then get some good sleep as well.

856
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:47,980
Actually, I've thought about it too.

857
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:54,460
That Yan Jicai
might actually be the killer.

858
00:36:08,550 --> 00:36:10,950
How often do you
get your physical checkup?

859
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:12,920
The unit arranges

860
00:36:13,550 --> 00:36:14,800
one once a year.

861
00:36:15,510 --> 00:36:17,110
Sometimes I'm too busy to go.

862
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,320
I'm fine, right?

863
00:36:21,510 --> 00:36:22,710
Where is your family?

864
00:36:23,150 --> 00:36:23,800
Doctor.

865
00:36:25,230 --> 00:36:25,840
You...

866
00:36:26,190 --> 00:36:27,320
You can just tell me.

867
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:30,550
I... I can take it.

868
00:36:42,770 --> 00:36:43,440
Why did you and your younger brother

869
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:44,840
get into a fight that day?

870
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:46,480
When?

871
00:36:48,030 --> 00:36:50,630
The night after the incident.

872
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:54,670
That morning, I went to pick him up

873
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:57,230
and only came home at night.

874
00:36:57,230 --> 00:36:58,480
After I got home,

875
00:36:58,920 --> 00:36:59,670
my dad told me

876
00:37:00,480 --> 00:37:02,010
that Yin Ping was murdered.

877
00:37:03,110 --> 00:37:03,970
My brother said

878
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:07,220
everyone would suspect that I'd done it.

879
00:37:07,230 --> 00:37:08,090
I got worked up,

880
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:09,840
and the two of us started fighting.

881
00:37:09,840 --> 00:37:11,590
Why did you get worked up
as soon as he said that?

882
00:37:11,590 --> 00:37:12,520
Feeling guilty?

883
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:13,960
The police

884
00:37:15,150 --> 00:37:16,480
asked me the same thing.

885
00:37:18,710 --> 00:37:19,480
The judge

886
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:21,210
might ask the same thing later.

887
00:37:22,190 --> 00:37:23,850
Wasn't I about to get married?

888
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:25,960
So my dad gave me

889
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:27,110
all the family savings.

890
00:37:27,110 --> 00:37:30,320
My brother had been
holding a grudge about it.

891
00:37:31,190 --> 00:37:32,470
And I've got a bad temper.

892
00:37:32,470 --> 00:37:33,800
I lose my temper easily.

893
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,290
So we started fighting.

894
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:36,520
How bad was the fight?

895
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:37,880
Was anyone seriously hurt?

896
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,320
My nose is delicate.

897
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:41,630
It's always bled easily since I was a kid.

898
00:37:41,630 --> 00:37:42,590
Whenever my brother and I fight,

899
00:37:42,590 --> 00:37:44,050
he always goes for my nose.

900
00:37:44,070 --> 00:37:45,440
All 3 of us were injured that day.

901
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:48,590
My dad even took a couple of punches
while trying to break us up.

902
00:37:48,590 --> 00:37:49,650
My brother has a bad temper.

903
00:37:49,650 --> 00:37:51,450
He gets worked up over the smallest thing.

904
00:37:51,450 --> 00:37:52,670
So there was blood from all 3 of you

905
00:37:52,670 --> 00:37:53,840
on this shirt,

906
00:37:53,840 --> 00:37:54,340
right?

907
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:55,640
I didn't notice that.

908
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:57,980
But the police said

909
00:37:59,030 --> 00:38:00,890
one of the blood types on the shirt

910
00:38:01,150 --> 00:38:02,960
matched Yin Ping's.

911
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:04,810
I think it was...

912
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:06,280
type A.

913
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:10,890
Who in your family has type A blood?

914
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:12,250
I think we're all type A.

915
00:38:15,250 --> 00:38:16,530
At the time, 3 buttons were found

916
00:38:16,530 --> 00:38:17,990
in the pocket of the shirt.

917
00:38:18,710 --> 00:38:19,840
Where did they come from?

918
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:22,500
Got torn off
when the three of us were grappling.

919
00:38:23,150 --> 00:38:23,840
My dad

920
00:38:24,880 --> 00:38:27,080
picked them up and put them in my pocket.

921
00:38:27,400 --> 00:38:30,000
A brand-new shirt,
and 3 buttons were torn off.

922
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:32,530
I had to crawl under the bed
to find all of them.

923
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:35,480
But in your statement, you said

924
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:36,550
the buttons were torn off by Yin Ping

925
00:38:36,550 --> 00:38:37,360
when he was resisting.

926
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,020
Whose side are you on, really?

927
00:38:40,150 --> 00:38:40,840
Are you here to help me

928
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:41,700
or to harm me?

929
00:38:42,630 --> 00:38:43,800
We're helping you

930
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:45,510
sort out the problems in your statement.

931
00:38:45,510 --> 00:38:46,570
Please cooperate.

932
00:38:46,920 --> 00:38:48,690
No, he doesn't know how to talk properly.

933
00:38:48,690 --> 00:38:50,320
If you don't know how to talk, go out.

934
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,190
Don't sit here.

935
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:56,040
Please forgive me for this.

936
00:39:00,670 --> 00:39:02,550
Alright, let's talk about the weapon.

937
00:39:02,550 --> 00:39:04,710
Where did you get that triangular bayonet?

938
00:39:04,710 --> 00:39:06,110
A fellow villager gave it to me.

939
00:39:06,110 --> 00:39:08,110
He wanted me to have it as a keepsake.

940
00:39:08,150 --> 00:39:10,030
He worked in the army managing supplies.

941
00:39:10,030 --> 00:39:12,030
So, it was a detachable part of a gun.

942
00:39:12,110 --> 00:39:12,770
Just great.

943
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:14,760
I've even dragged him down.

944
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:16,150
So where did you usually keep it?

945
00:39:16,150 --> 00:39:16,760
At home?

946
00:39:17,230 --> 00:39:18,320
I wrapped it in oiled paper

947
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,480
and put it under the bed.

948
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,640
I didn't dare to take it out.

949
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:22,040
So when the police

950
00:39:22,070 --> 00:39:23,320
found it during the search,

951
00:39:23,320 --> 00:39:24,280
the bayonet was

952
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:25,810
coated with gun oil, right?

953
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:27,640
It wasn't gun oil. It was grease.

954
00:39:28,210 --> 00:39:28,880
The kind of grease

955
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:29,940
used on machinery.

956
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:32,870
Wait, well...

957
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:35,590
The police insisted that I used it

958
00:39:35,590 --> 00:39:36,990
to stab Yin Ping to death.

959
00:39:37,030 --> 00:39:37,890
I'm not stupid.

960
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:39,410
Why would I bring

961
00:39:39,550 --> 00:39:40,920
the murder weapon home
after killing someone?

962
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,550
And even wipe it clean, oil it,

963
00:39:42,550 --> 00:39:43,630
and wrap it up again.

964
00:39:43,630 --> 00:39:46,050
Just wait for the police
to come search my house?

965
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:47,280
Then how were those statements

966
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:48,620
made in the first place?

967
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:54,480
Try going

968
00:39:54,510 --> 00:39:56,150
without sleep for days and nights,

969
00:39:56,150 --> 00:39:57,280
and see how you talk.

970
00:39:57,880 --> 00:39:59,880
He only seems to talk to me like this.

971
00:40:25,190 --> 00:40:25,760
Here?

972
00:40:26,030 --> 00:40:26,480
Yes.

973
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:28,960
Sir,

974
00:40:29,550 --> 00:40:30,750
w-what are you doing?

975
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:32,610
Filling the canal to build a road.

976
00:40:32,610 --> 00:40:33,320
Take a break.

977
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:34,020
Fill the canal to build a road.

978
00:40:34,020 --> 00:40:35,170
Well, does the public security bureau

979
00:40:35,170 --> 00:40:36,190
know about this?

980
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:38,920
Since when does the public security bureau
handle road repairs?

981
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:39,880
Who are you?

982
00:40:42,030 --> 00:40:42,890
We're lawyers.

983
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:44,320
Here's my business card.

984
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:48,030
Are you guys...

985
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:50,140
responsible for this whole area?

986
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:51,930
We take turns working here.

987
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:53,470
What, what's the matter?

988
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:54,840
Have you ever

989
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:56,440
dug up anything around here?

990
00:40:56,510 --> 00:40:57,710
What could we dig up here?

991
00:40:57,710 --> 00:40:58,360
Gold?

992
00:40:59,130 --> 00:41:00,720
I mean, l-like

993
00:41:00,760 --> 00:41:02,610
a screwdriver, a knife,
or something like that.

994
00:41:02,610 --> 00:41:04,010
Have you found anything?

995
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:07,230
I know why you're here.

996
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:10,050
There was a murder in this area.

997
00:41:10,230 --> 00:41:11,710
A nutcase was stabbed to death.

998
00:41:11,710 --> 00:41:13,280
And an old woman hanged herself.

999
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:14,670
We heard about it before we came here.

1000
00:41:14,670 --> 00:41:15,760
Are you here for that?

1001
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:16,070
Yes.

1002
00:41:16,510 --> 00:41:17,630
Lawyers...

1003
00:41:18,050 --> 00:41:19,440
Are lawyers even investigating cases now?

1004
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,500
Isn't that the police's job?

1005
00:41:20,500 --> 00:41:22,170
Well, we're authorized

1006
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:23,510
by the procuratorate to investigate.

1007
00:41:23,510 --> 00:41:25,040
It's officially approved.

1008
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:26,560
Here, man.

1009
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:28,960
Have a cigarette.

1010
00:41:33,190 --> 00:41:34,000
Have one more. Come on.

1011
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:34,460
Come on.

1012
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:36,120
Well,

1013
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:37,630
could you help us keep an ear out?

1014
00:41:37,630 --> 00:41:38,550
And if anyone

1015
00:41:38,550 --> 00:41:39,480
finds anything,

1016
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:40,230
could you

1017
00:41:40,230 --> 00:41:40,960
give us a call?

1018
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:41,800
If we really find something,

1019
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:43,420
shouldn't we call the police?

1020
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:45,080
You think I don't know the law?

1021
00:41:46,150 --> 00:41:47,590
Then, did the police come here before?

1022
00:41:47,590 --> 00:41:48,450
Never saw them.

1023
00:41:49,110 --> 00:41:49,960
Well, come on.

1024
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:51,300
Take this pack.

1025
00:41:51,630 --> 00:41:52,510
You should

1026
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:53,920
definitely call the police first.

1027
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:55,110
Then give us a call

1028
00:41:55,110 --> 00:41:55,770
afterward.

1029
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,800
T-There are phone numbers on it.

1030
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:07,800
Turn off the flashlight.

1031
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:14,860
H-How are we supposed to
find them like this?

1032
00:42:19,190 --> 00:42:19,950
Can you see?

1033
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:21,510
Nothing.

1034
00:42:21,530 --> 00:42:23,130
I can't see anything either.

1035
00:42:40,840 --> 00:42:41,300
Come on.

1036
00:42:41,910 --> 00:42:42,510
Shine a light.

1037
00:42:42,510 --> 00:42:43,440
Look, is this it?

1038
00:42:47,550 --> 00:42:47,950
Right?

1039
00:42:49,710 --> 00:42:50,770
How long's it been?

1040
00:42:53,030 --> 00:42:53,890
Fifty minutes.

1041
00:42:54,030 --> 00:42:55,030
Fifty minutes...

1042
00:42:57,060 --> 00:42:58,800
At this rate, wouldn't finding
all 3 of them take all night?

1043
00:42:58,800 --> 00:43:00,960
We'd be looking until tomorrow morning.

1044
00:43:00,960 --> 00:43:01,670
Are you still looking?

1045
00:43:01,670 --> 00:43:02,480
You go find one.
